<pre class=metadata>
Title: Regional Preference Media Queries
Shortname: regional-preference-media-queries
Level: none
Status: LD
ED: https://arronei.github.io/CSS-Additions/system-media-queries/regional-preferences/spec/
Repository: arronei/CSS-Additions
Editor: Arron Eicholz
Abstract: This specification adds media features for four regional preferences: '@media/hour-cycle' (a 12- or
    24-hour clock), '@media/measurement-system' (metric, UK, or US units), '@media/temperature-unit'
    (Celsius or Fahrenheit), and '@media/first-day-of-week'. A page can show times, distances, temperatures,
    and calendars the way the user reads them without script. The values always match what
    <code>Intl</code> gives script in the same document, so they reveal nothing new to script; where there is
    no script, they come only from the language the browser already sends to servers; and they never change
    while a document is open.
Markup Shorthands: markdown yes, css yes
Complain About: accidental-2119 no, missing-example-ids yes
Assume Explicit For: yes
</pre>

